# RushDay API — every route, grouped by surface. Start the API with scripts/run-api.ps1 (never dotnet run).
#
# Every non-GET /api request needs the X-CSRF-TOKEN header (D5); its value arrives only in JSON, never a readable
# cookie: from GET /api/auth/csrf before signing in, and from the login/mfa-verify/me responses afterwards. This
# file relies on your REST client's cookie jar to carry the session cookie automatically between requests (VS
# Code's REST Client and most others do this per file/host); it never sets Cookie by hand.
#
# The three role blocks below each start with their own csrf -> login pair. Run a block top to bottom; switching
# blocks (student -> lecturer -> admin) replaces the active session, which is expected — sign in again if you jump
# back to an earlier block out of order.

@RushDay_HostAddress = http://localhost:5080

### JSON index (story, links, deployed commit)
GET {{RushDay_HostAddress}}/api

### Liveness (Render's health check; no database access; unlimited)
GET {{RushDay_HostAddress}}/api/health/live

### Readiness (database reachability; rate-limited per address)
GET {{RushDay_HostAddress}}/api/health/ready

### Public status (demo accounts only when Demo:Enabled; the latest and next results publication)
GET {{RushDay_HostAddress}}/api/public/status

### Unknown API route: JSON 404, never index.html
GET {{RushDay_HostAddress}}/api/nope


########################################################################################################
# SESSION FLOW (anonymous) — csrf -> login -> me -> change-password -> logout, and the antiforgery check
########################################################################################################

### 1. Anonymous antiforgery token (sets the rushday.csrf cookie)
# @name anonCsrf
GET {{RushDay_HostAddress}}/api/auth/csrf

### 2. A mutation without the X-CSRF-TOKEN header is refused: 400 urn:rushday:antiforgery
POST {{RushDay_HostAddress}}/api/auth/logout

### 3. POST /api/auth/register does not exist: 404 ProblemDetails, not 401 (no self-registration, D1)
POST {{RushDay_HostAddress}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{anonCsrf.response.body.$.csrfToken}}

{}


########################################################################################################
# STUDENT — sign in as S000001 and walk /api/me, /api/modules, /api/announcements
########################################################################################################

### Student: csrf
# @name studentCsrf
GET {{RushDay_HostAddress}}/api/auth/csrf

### Student: login (answers Me directly — S000001 has no second factor)
# @name studentLogin
POST {{RushDay_HostAddress}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{studentCsrf.response.body.$.csrfToken}}

{
  "username": "S000001",
  "password": "Student-Demo-2026!"
}

### Who am I (a fresh token bound to this identity; also refreshes the token after any of the calls below)
# @name studentMe
GET {{RushDay_HostAddress}}/api/auth/me

### Dashboard: name, programme, modules, completed modules, results, timetable, windows, announcements — 5 queries
GET {{RushDay_HostAddress}}/api/me/dashboard

### Results by year and semester (scheduled instants shown for anything not yet published)
GET {{RushDay_HostAddress}}/api/me/results

### This week's timetable (current semester only)
GET {{RushDay_HostAddress}}/api/me/timetable

### My enrolments (current and completed, with withdraw eligibility per row)
GET {{RushDay_HostAddress}}/api/me/enrolments

### Personal data export (audited: student.exported_self)
GET {{RushDay_HostAddress}}/api/me/export.json

### Module catalogue (viewer-agnostic list, cached 30s; my own state comes from /api/me/enrolments instead)
GET {{RushDay_HostAddress}}/api/modules

### Module detail (uncached; live placesRemaining)
GET {{RushDay_HostAddress}}/api/modules/CS3099

### Announcements visible to me (university-wide plus my modules' own)
GET {{RushDay_HostAddress}}/api/announcements

### Enrol on CS3099 (30 places; expect 201, or 409 module-full once it fills)
# @name studentEnrol
POST {{RushDay_HostAddress}}/api/me/enrolments
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{studentMe.response.body.$.csrfToken}}

{
  "moduleCode": "CS3099"
}

### Withdraw from CS3099 (before the withdrawal deadline, no submitted/published mark)
DELETE {{RushDay_HostAddress}}/api/me/enrolments/CS3099
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{studentMe.response.body.$.csrfToken}}

### Change password (forced for a freshly provisioned or reset account). Demo accounts are read-only (D7), so this
### answers 409 demo-account against S000001 on the public demo; it succeeds for a real, provisioned account.
POST {{RushDay_HostAddress}}/api/auth/change-password
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{studentMe.response.body.$.csrfToken}}

{
  "currentPassword": "Student-Demo-2026!",
  "newPassword": "Student-Demo-2026!"
}

### Sign out (rotates the security stamp: every session of the account ends)
POST {{RushDay_HostAddress}}/api/auth/logout
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{studentMe.response.body.$.csrfToken}}


########################################################################################################
# LECTURER — sign in as L00001 and walk /api/lecturer (module leader on CS3001 and CS3099)
########################################################################################################

### Lecturer: csrf
# @name lecturerCsrf
GET {{RushDay_HostAddress}}/api/auth/csrf

### Lecturer: login
# @name lecturerLogin
POST {{RushDay_HostAddress}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{lecturerCsrf.response.body.$.csrfToken}}

{
  "username": "L00001",
  "password": "Lecturer-Demo-2026!"
}

### Who am I
# @name lecturerMe
GET {{RushDay_HostAddress}}/api/auth/me

### My modules (this year's enrolled count, capacity, marks status)
GET {{RushDay_HostAddress}}/api/lecturer/modules

### Roster for CS3001 (paged, searched by number prefix or name fragment)
GET {{RushDay_HostAddress}}/api/lecturer/modules/CS3001/roster?page=1&pageSize=50

### Roster for CS3001 as CSV (RFC 4180, CSV-injection-safe cells)
GET {{RushDay_HostAddress}}/api/lecturer/modules/CS3001/roster.csv
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{lecturerMe.response.body.$.csrfToken}}

### Marks sheet for CS3001 (paged editable grid of drafts)
GET {{RushDay_HostAddress}}/api/lecturer/modules/CS3001/marks?page=1&pageSize=100

### Save marks (all-or-nothing per request; version is the optimistic-concurrency stamp of a row you have already seen)
# @name lecturerSaveMarks
PUT {{RushDay_HostAddress}}/api/lecturer/modules/CS3001/marks
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{lecturerMe.response.body.$.csrfToken}}

{
  "rows": [
    { "studentNumber": "S000001", "mark": 72, "outcome": "mark" },
    { "studentNumber": "S000004", "outcome": "absent" }
  ]
}

### Submit CS3001 (module leader only; 422 lists missing students if any active enrolment lacks a mark/outcome)
POST {{RushDay_HostAddress}}/api/lecturer/modules/CS3001/marks/submit
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{lecturerMe.response.body.$.csrfToken}}

### Module announcements for CS3001
GET {{RushDay_HostAddress}}/api/lecturer/modules/CS3001/announcements

### Create a module announcement
# @name lecturerCreateAnnouncement
POST {{RushDay_HostAddress}}/api/lecturer/modules/CS3001/announcements
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{lecturerMe.response.body.$.csrfToken}}

{
  "title": "Office hours this week",
  "body": "I will hold office hours on Thursday 14:00-15:00 in E14, room 2.03.",
  "pinned": false
}

### Update that announcement
PUT {{RushDay_HostAddress}}/api/lecturer/modules/CS3001/announcements/{{lecturerCreateAnnouncement.response.body.$.id}}
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{lecturerMe.response.body.$.csrfToken}}

{
  "title": "Office hours this week (room changed)",
  "body": "I will hold office hours on Thursday 14:00-15:00 in E14, room 2.05.",
  "pinned": true
}

### Delete that announcement
DELETE {{RushDay_HostAddress}}/api/lecturer/modules/CS3001/announcements/{{lecturerCreateAnnouncement.response.body.$.id}}
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{lecturerMe.response.body.$.csrfToken}}

### Cross-role check: a lecturer on an admin route is 403, not a redirect or a 404
GET {{RushDay_HostAddress}}/api/admin/overview

### Sign out
POST {{RushDay_HostAddress}}/api/auth/logout
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{lecturerMe.response.body.$.csrfToken}}


########################################################################################################
# ADMINISTRATOR — sign in as admin (MFA-exempt only in demo mode) and walk /api/admin
########################################################################################################

### Admin: csrf
# @name adminCsrf
GET {{RushDay_HostAddress}}/api/auth/csrf

### Admin: login (demo admin is MFA-exempt while Demo:Enabled; a real admin gets { mfaRequired: true } here instead)
# @name adminLogin
POST {{RushDay_HostAddress}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{adminCsrf.response.body.$.csrfToken}}

{
  "username": "admin",
  "password": "Admin-Demo-2026!"
}

### If MFA is required instead of Me, verify with a 6-digit TOTP code (uncomment and fill in)
# POST {{RushDay_HostAddress}}/api/auth/mfa/verify
# Content-Type: application/json
# X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{adminLogin.response.body.$.csrfToken}}
#
# {
#   "code": "123456"
# }

### Who am I
# @name adminMe
GET {{RushDay_HostAddress}}/api/auth/me

### --- MFA setup (a real, non-demo administrator without a second factor is gated to these routes only) ---
### Demo accounts cannot be given a second factor (D7): both calls below answer 409 demo-account for the demo
### `admin`. Provision a non-demo administrator first (Bootstrap:AdminPassword, or an account you create while demo
### mode is off) to see this flow actually complete.

### Start MFA setup (a shared key and an otpauth:// URI for an authenticator app)
# @name mfaSetup
POST {{RushDay_HostAddress}}/api/auth/mfa/setup
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{adminMe.response.body.$.csrfToken}}

### Enable MFA with a code from that shared key
POST {{RushDay_HostAddress}}/api/auth/mfa/enable
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{adminMe.response.body.$.csrfToken}}

{
  "code": "123456"
}

### --- Overview ---

### Overview: counts, windows, publications, submission progress, recent audit, database health
GET {{RushDay_HostAddress}}/api/admin/overview

### Ops snapshot: request rate, p95/p99, error rate, load shedding, pool usage, memory (outside the global limiter)
GET {{RushDay_HostAddress}}/api/admin/ops/metrics

### Reconcile enrolled_count against active current-year enrolments (also runs at every startup and settings change)
POST {{RushDay_HostAddress}}/api/admin/ops/reconcile
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{adminMe.response.body.$.csrfToken}}

### Demo reset: withdraw CS3099's self-enrolments-without-a-mark on demand (demo mode only; 404 otherwise)
POST {{RushDay_HostAddress}}/api/admin/ops/demo-reset
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{adminMe.response.body.$.csrfToken}}

### --- Settings ---

### Current settings
GET {{RushDay_HostAddress}}/api/admin/settings

### Update settings (a changed academicYear recomputes enrolledCount for the whole catalogue)
PUT {{RushDay_HostAddress}}/api/admin/settings
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{adminMe.response.body.$.csrfToken}}

{
  "academicYear": "2026/27",
  "currentSemester": "autumn",
  "institutionName": "RushDay Demo University",
  "institutionShortName": "RushDay",
  "timeZone": "Europe/London",
  "supportEmail": "support@example.ac.uk",
  "supportUrl": "https://example.ac.uk/support"
}

### --- Enrolment windows ---

### List windows
GET {{RushDay_HostAddress}}/api/admin/enrolment-windows

### Create a window
# @name createWindow
POST {{RushDay_HostAddress}}/api/admin/enrolment-windows
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{adminMe.response.body.$.csrfToken}}

{
  "academicYear": "2027/28",
  "semester": "autumn",
  "opensAt": "2027-09-13T09:00:00Z",
  "closesAt": "2027-10-01T17:00:00Z",
  "withdrawalDeadlineAt": "2027-10-29T17:00:00Z"
}

### Update that window
PUT {{RushDay_HostAddress}}/api/admin/enrolment-windows/{{createWindow.response.body.$.id}}
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{adminMe.response.body.$.csrfToken}}

{
  "opensAt": "2027-09-13T09:00:00Z",
  "closesAt": "2027-10-03T17:00:00Z",
  "withdrawalDeadlineAt": "2027-10-31T17:00:00Z"
}

### Delete that window
DELETE {{RushDay_HostAddress}}/api/admin/enrolment-windows/{{createWindow.response.body.$.id}}
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{adminMe.response.body.$.csrfToken}}

### --- Results ---

### Submission progress for Autumn of the current year
GET {{RushDay_HostAddress}}/api/admin/results?semester=autumn

### Publish Autumn 2026/27 (publishAt must be at most 90 days ahead of now — adjust the date below if it has aged
### past that window; 422 publish-too-far-ahead means it needs to move closer). This answers 409 nothing-to-publish
### until at least one module of the semester is fully Submitted: the marks-entry example above only entered one of
### CS3001's 100 students, which is not enough to submit it. Follow "Re-run results day on the demo" in
### docs/admin-guide.md for the complete recipe (enter every mark, submit, then publish).
# @name publish
POST {{RushDay_HostAddress}}/api/admin/results/publish
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{adminMe.response.body.$.csrfToken}}

{
  "academicYear": "2026/27",
  "semester": "autumn",
  "publishAt": "2026-10-15T09:00:00Z",
  "announce": true,
  "note": "Results day, re-run on the demo (docs/admin-guide.md)."
}

### Reschedule that publication (only while it is still scheduled, publishAt in the future)
PUT {{RushDay_HostAddress}}/api/admin/results/publications/{{publish.response.body.$.publication.id}}
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{adminMe.response.body.$.csrfToken}}

{
  "publishAt": "2027-01-01T10:00:00Z"
}

### Cancel that scheduled publication (grades revert to Submitted)
DELETE {{RushDay_HostAddress}}/api/admin/results/publications/{{publish.response.body.$.publication.id}}
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{adminMe.response.body.$.csrfToken}}

### Unpublish a live publication with a reason (use a publication id that is actually live)
# POST {{RushDay_HostAddress}}/api/admin/results/publications/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/unpublish
# Content-Type: application/json
# X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{adminMe.response.body.$.csrfToken}}
#
# {
#   "reason": "Exam board asked for a recheck before release."
# }

### Return CS3001 to draft with a reason (allowed before or during a scheduled publication)
POST {{RushDay_HostAddress}}/api/admin/results/modules/CS3001/return-to-draft
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{adminMe.response.body.$.csrfToken}}

{
  "reason": "A mark needs correcting before the exam board signs off on this module."
}

### Correct a single mark (submitted or published)
POST {{RushDay_HostAddress}}/api/admin/results/modules/CS3001/marks/S000001/correct
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{adminMe.response.body.$.csrfToken}}

{
  "mark": 75,
  "outcome": "mark",
  "reason": "Marking error found on re-check: three marks were transposed on the original sheet."
}

### --- Students ---

### List/search students
GET {{RushDay_HostAddress}}/api/admin/students?q=S00000

### Create a student
POST {{RushDay_HostAddress}}/api/admin/students
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{adminMe.response.body.$.csrfToken}}

{
  "studentNumber": "S099999",
  "fullName": "Test Student",
  "programme": "BSc Computer Science",
  "yearOfStudy": 1,
  "email": "test.student@example.ac.uk"
}

### View a student as the student sees it, plus account state (audited: student.viewed)
GET {{RushDay_HostAddress}}/api/admin/students/S099999

### Update a student
PUT {{RushDay_HostAddress}}/api/admin/students/S099999
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{adminMe.response.body.$.csrfToken}}

{
  "fullName": "Test Student",
  "programme": "BSc Computer Science",
  "yearOfStudy": 2,
  "email": "test.student@example.ac.uk"
}

### Export a student's data on the academic office's behalf (audited: student.exported)
GET {{RushDay_HostAddress}}/api/admin/students/S099999/export.json

### Override-enrol (ignores the window and credit limit; capacity still applies unless forceCapacity raises it by one)
POST {{RushDay_HostAddress}}/api/admin/students/S099999/enrolments
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{adminMe.response.body.$.csrfToken}}

{
  "moduleCode": "CS3001",
  "reason": "Late transfer from another programme, approved by the programme lead.",
  "forceCapacity": false
}

### Override-withdraw with a reason
POST {{RushDay_HostAddress}}/api/admin/students/S099999/enrolments/CS3001/withdraw
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{adminMe.response.body.$.csrfToken}}

{
  "reason": "Student confirmed they meant to enrol on CS3099, not CS3001."
}

### Mark a student as left (withdraws this year's enrolments, disables the account)
POST {{RushDay_HostAddress}}/api/admin/students/S099999/leave
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{adminMe.response.body.$.csrfToken}}

{
  "reason": "Withdrew from the university, confirmed by the registry."
}

### --- Modules ---

### List modules (includeInactive to also see retired ones)
GET {{RushDay_HostAddress}}/api/admin/modules?includeInactive=false

### Create a module
POST {{RushDay_HostAddress}}/api/admin/modules
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{adminMe.response.body.$.csrfToken}}

{
  "code": "ZZ1001",
  "title": "Test Module",
  "description": "A module created for exercising RushDay.Api.http.",
  "credits": 15,
  "capacity": 30,
  "semester": "autumn"
}

### Update it (capacity is never lowered below enrolledCount; an unchanged capacity is always accepted)
PUT {{RushDay_HostAddress}}/api/admin/modules/ZZ1001
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{adminMe.response.body.$.csrfToken}}

{
  "title": "Test Module",
  "description": "A module created for exercising RushDay.Api.http.",
  "credits": 15,
  "capacity": 40,
  "semester": "autumn",
  "isActive": true
}

### Read-only roster of any module (registry access, D33)
GET {{RushDay_HostAddress}}/api/admin/modules/CS3001/roster

### Read-only marks sheet of any module
GET {{RushDay_HostAddress}}/api/admin/modules/CS3001/marks

### Assign lecturers (exactly one leader; nobody who has left)
PUT {{RushDay_HostAddress}}/api/admin/modules/ZZ1001/lecturers
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{adminMe.response.body.$.csrfToken}}

{
  "assignments": [
    { "staffNumber": "L00001", "role": "leader" }
  ]
}

### Trim an over-capacity module back to its capacity, with a reason
POST {{RushDay_HostAddress}}/api/admin/modules/ZZ1001/trim-to-capacity
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{adminMe.response.body.$.csrfToken}}

{
  "reason": "Correcting drift inherited from a earlier manual data fix."
}

### --- Lecturers ---

### List/search lecturers
GET {{RushDay_HostAddress}}/api/admin/lecturers?q=Khan

### Create a lecturer
POST {{RushDay_HostAddress}}/api/admin/lecturers
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{adminMe.response.body.$.csrfToken}}

{
  "staffNumber": "L00099",
  "fullName": "Test Lecturer",
  "title": "Dr",
  "department": "CS",
  "email": "test.lecturer@example.ac.uk"
}

### Update a lecturer
PUT {{RushDay_HostAddress}}/api/admin/lecturers/L00099
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{adminMe.response.body.$.csrfToken}}

{
  "fullName": "Test Lecturer",
  "title": "Prof",
  "department": "CS",
  "email": "test.lecturer@example.ac.uk"
}

### Mark a lecturer as left
POST {{RushDay_HostAddress}}/api/admin/lecturers/L00099/leave
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{adminMe.response.body.$.csrfToken}}

{
  "reason": "Left the university at the end of the academic year."
}

### --- Accounts ---
### Note: while signed in as the demo `admin`, anything you provision here is itself made a demo account (a demo
### actor can only ever create more demo data, never a real one) and demo accounts are read-only — lock/unlock/
### disable/enable/reset-mfa/reset-password below will each answer 409 demo-account against it. That is correct
### product behaviour, not a bug in this file: run the same sequence as a non-demo administrator to see them succeed.

### List/search accounts
GET {{RushDay_HostAddress}}/api/admin/accounts?role=Student&state=active

### Provision an account for the existing student S099999 (a temporary password shown once; omit temporaryPassword
### to have one generated). studentNumber/staffNumber is required exactly when role is Student/Lecturer, and must
### name a student/lecturer record that already exists (create one first, see the Students section above).
# @name provisionAccount
POST {{RushDay_HostAddress}}/api/admin/accounts
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{adminMe.response.body.$.csrfToken}}

{
  "username": "S099999",
  "displayName": "Test Student",
  "role": "Student",
  "studentNumber": "S099999"
}

### Lock the account
POST {{RushDay_HostAddress}}/api/admin/accounts/{{provisionAccount.response.body.$.account.id}}/lock
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{adminMe.response.body.$.csrfToken}}

### Unlock it
POST {{RushDay_HostAddress}}/api/admin/accounts/{{provisionAccount.response.body.$.account.id}}/unlock
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{adminMe.response.body.$.csrfToken}}

### Disable it
POST {{RushDay_HostAddress}}/api/admin/accounts/{{provisionAccount.response.body.$.account.id}}/disable
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{adminMe.response.body.$.csrfToken}}

### Enable it again
POST {{RushDay_HostAddress}}/api/admin/accounts/{{provisionAccount.response.body.$.account.id}}/enable
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{adminMe.response.body.$.csrfToken}}

### Reset its second factor (an administrator's lost authenticator device)
POST {{RushDay_HostAddress}}/api/admin/accounts/{{provisionAccount.response.body.$.account.id}}/reset-mfa
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{adminMe.response.body.$.csrfToken}}

### Reset its password (sets must-change-password; body is optional, a password is generated when omitted)
POST {{RushDay_HostAddress}}/api/admin/accounts/{{provisionAccount.response.body.$.account.id}}/reset-password
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{adminMe.response.body.$.csrfToken}}

{}

### --- University announcements ---

### List
GET {{RushDay_HostAddress}}/api/admin/announcements

### Create a university-wide announcement
# @name createUniAnnouncement
POST {{RushDay_HostAddress}}/api/admin/announcements
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{adminMe.response.body.$.csrfToken}}

{
  "title": "Library extended hours during exams",
  "body": "The main library is open 24 hours from 1 to 19 December.",
  "pinned": false
}

### Update it
PUT {{RushDay_HostAddress}}/api/admin/announcements/{{createUniAnnouncement.response.body.$.id}}
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{adminMe.response.body.$.csrfToken}}

{
  "title": "Library extended hours during exams (updated)",
  "body": "The main library is open 24 hours from 1 to 20 December.",
  "pinned": true
}

### Delete it
DELETE {{RushDay_HostAddress}}/api/admin/announcements/{{createUniAnnouncement.response.body.$.id}}
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{adminMe.response.body.$.csrfToken}}

### --- Audit ---

### Filtered audit log
GET {{RushDay_HostAddress}}/api/admin/audit?action=enrolment.created&page=1&pageSize=50

### CSV export (itself audited: audit.exported; truncation is signalled with a trailing comment line)
GET {{RushDay_HostAddress}}/api/admin/audit/export.csv
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{adminMe.response.body.$.csrfToken}}

### --- Cross-role checks ---

### An administrator on a lecturer-only route is 403, not a silent pass-through
GET {{RushDay_HostAddress}}/api/lecturer/modules

### Sign out (rotates the security stamp: every session of this account ends)
POST {{RushDay_HostAddress}}/api/auth/logout
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{adminMe.response.body.$.csrfToken}}
